<section>
  <exercises>
    <heading level="1">Section 1.5 Exercises</heading>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, determine the equation of the parabola using the information given.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="255" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Focus $$\left( {4,0} \right)$$ and directrix $$x = -4$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y 2 = 16 x y 2 = 16 x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="256" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Focus $$\left( {0,-3} \right)$$ and directrix $$y = 3$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="257" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Focus $$\left( {0,0.5} \right)$$ and directrix $$y = -0.5$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 2 = 2 y x 2 = 2 y$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="258" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Focus $$\left( {2, 3} \right)$$ and directrix $$x = -2$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="259" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Focus $$\left( {0,2} \right)$$ and directrix $$y = 4$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 2 = -4 ( y - 3 ) x 2 = -4 ( y - 3 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="260" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Focus $$\left( {-1,4} \right)$$ and directrix $$x = 5$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="261" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Focus $$\left( {-3,5} \right)$$ and directrix $$y = 1$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( x + 3 ) 2 = 8 ( y - 3 ) ( x + 3 ) 2 = 8 ( y - 3 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="262" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Focus $$\left( {\frac{5}{2},-4} \right)$$ and directrix $$x = \frac{7}{2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, determine the equation of the ellipse using the information given.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="263" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Endpoints of major axis at $$\left( {4,0} \right),\left( {-4,0} \right)$$ and foci located at $$\left( {2,0} \right),\left( {-2,0} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 2 16 + y 2 12 = 1 x 2 16 + y 2 12 = 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="264" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Endpoints of major axis at $$\left( {0,5} \right),\left( {0,-5} \right)$$ and foci located at $$\left( {0,3} \right),\left( {0,-3} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="265" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Endpoints of minor axis at $$\left( {0,2} \right),\left( {0,-2} \right)$$ and foci located at $$\left( {3,0} \right),\left( {-3,0} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 2 13 + y 2 4 = 1 x 2 13 + y 2 4 = 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="266" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Endpoints of major axis at $$\left( {-3,3} \right),\left( {7,3} \right)$$ and foci located at $$\left( {-2,3} \right),\left( {6,3} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="267" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Endpoints of major axis at $$\left( {-3,5} \right),\left( {-3,-3} \right)$$ and foci located at $$\left( {-3,3} \right),\left( {-3,-1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( y - 1 ) 2 16 + ( x + 3 ) 2 12 = 1 ( y - 1 ) 2 16 + ( x + 3 ) 2 12 = 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="268" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Endpoints of major axis at $$\left( {0,0} \right),\left( {0,4} \right)$$ and foci located at $$\left( {5,2} \right),\left( {-5,2} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="269" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Foci located at $$\left( {2,0} \right), \left( {-2,0} \right)$$ and eccentricity of $$\frac{1}{2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 2 16 + y 2 12 = 1 x 2 16 + y 2 12 = 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="270" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Foci located at $$\left( {0,-3} \right), \left( {0,3} \right)$$ and eccentricity of $$\frac{3}{4}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, determine the equation of the hyperbola using the information given.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="271" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Vertices located at $$\left( {5,0} \right),\left( {-5,0} \right)$$ and foci located at $$\left( {6,0} \right),\left( {-6,0} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 2 25 - y 2 11 = 1 x 2 25 - y 2 11 = 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="272" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Vertices located at $$\left( {0,2} \right),\left( {0,-2} \right)$$ and foci located at $$\left( {0,3} \right),\left( {0,-3} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="273" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Endpoints of the conjugate axis located at $$\left( {0,3} \right),\left( {0,-3} \right)$$ and foci located $$\left( {4,0} \right),\left( {-4,0} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 2 7 - y 2 9 = 1 x 2 7 - y 2 9 = 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="274" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Vertices located at $$\left( {0,1} \right),\left( {6,1} \right)$$ and focus located at $$\left( {8,1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="275" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Vertices located at $$\left( {-2,0} \right),\left( {-2,-4} \right)$$ and focus located at $$\left( {-2,-8} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( y + 2 ) 2 4 - ( x + 2 ) 2 32 = 1 ( y + 2 ) 2 4 - ( x + 2 ) 2 32 = 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="276" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Endpoints of the conjugate axis located at $$\left( {3,2} \right),\left( {3,4} \right)$$ and focus located at $$\left( {3,7} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="277" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Foci located at $$( - 6,0),(6,0)$$ and eccentricity of 3</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 2 4 - y 2 32 = 1 x 2 4 - y 2 32 = 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="278" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {0,10} \right),\left( {0,-10} \right)$$ and eccentricity of 2.5</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, consider the following polar equations of conics. Determine the eccentricity and identify the conic.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="279" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$r = \frac{-1}{1 + \cos \theta}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$e=1,e=1,$$ parabola</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="280" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$r = \frac{8}{2 - \sin \theta}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="281" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$r = \frac{5}{2 + \sin \theta}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$e=12,e=12,$$ ellipse</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="282" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$r = \frac{5}{-1 + 2 \sin \theta}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="283" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$r = \frac{3}{2 - 6 \sin \theta}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$e=3,e=3,$$ hyperbola</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="284" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$r = \frac{3}{-4 + 3 \sin \theta}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, find a polar equation of the conic with focus at the origin and eccentricity and directrix as given.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="285" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\text{Directrix:} x = 4;e = \frac{1}{5}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$r = 4 5 + cos \theta r = 4 5 + cos \theta$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="286" has_solution="false">
